message: "If you use this tool, its data or its analysis plan, please cite it as below."
title: "Where to invest against TB in India: a State and district priority tool"
abstract: >-
  Code, extracted data, outputs and a pre-registered analysis plan for a tool
  that shows where closing a gap in India's TB care pathway would avert the most
  harm, counted as patients lost at each step (shortfall against target, not
  tested for rifampicin resistance, died, lost to follow-up, DR-TB treatment not
  successful, HIV status not known), with uncertainty, tiers rather than ranks,
  and a rising-risk flag from each gap's trend. It uses published, aggregate
  India TB Report tables for States and UTs (data years 2018-2023), tests the
  stability of the priorities over time and their association with the ICMR
  National TB Prevalence Survey, and demonstrates the same functions on district
  tables. Observational; no causal estimates.
